{"seq":16,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T07:55:00.556Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"bccaafdf371638bcdf2f82698b5509f6aa14acf818fc451bb6cf0405fac3fd6a","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes that you can see (the North and Central team digests). I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025: the gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard wasn't sending SMS bay assignments to drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the next shift got through without problems. The note also says the kiosk logs should be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThere are no QFL ticket numbers in Moss's 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest or the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoff digest are for Marrow accounts, not QFL. Also, the cheat sheet points out that Quarendon Freightways is a different company and not a customer, so keep it out of the list.\n\nOne more thing: the #4419 note is undated, so I can't tell you how current it is."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
